Z||000000||Pyric||12-14-2001||06:49 AM||||Okay, so I order an intake manifold set from carparts.com because all I needed was the Plenum gaskets, and I figured since it was called an "INTAKE MANIFOLD SET" that it would include all, or most of the gaskets for the entire intake manifold.<P>Did it?  NO!!!!!!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smiley-angry.gif">  <P>ALL it came with was the bottom gasket for the MIDDLE manifold.  WHAT THE HELL IS THAT?  That isn't a set, that is a pair.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>So I checked at other places and all they have is the same 2 gaskets for it.  Is there a special name for the V6 plenum gaskets? or are the parts places just stupid.<P>PS.  Here is a pic of all I got, <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/gasket.jpg">  <BR>and I didn't even get the return invoice with it when the sent it.  Bastages!!!<P>Sorry, had to vent.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieronegS.jpg">    <P><BR>"Never offend people with style when you can offend them with substance." <BR>--Sam Brown<p>[This message has been edited by Pyric (edited 12-14-2001).]||||reg||8
Z||000001||Rodrv6||12-14-2001||09:10 AM||||Oh, the joys of online ordering!!!<BR>Those look like the gaskets between the lower intake and the cylinder heads.  I got a set of plenum gaskets at the local parts store.  Their listing was for "plenum gaskets", not "intake gaskets".  It was a Fel-Pro set and had everything except for the fuel injector "0" rings.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  <BR>White 88 GT :)||||reg||1
Z||000002||Pyric||12-14-2001||09:31 AM||||Yeah none of the online parts stores had the plenum gaskets labeled that way.  They only had one set of "Intake gaskets" and this was it.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Edited cuz I can't spell  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Pyric (edited 12-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroJoe||12-14-2001||10:23 AM||||I dont even bother trying to find parts on carparts.com or wrenchhead.com  All the descriptions never really tell you what you're going to be getting, and the prices are actaully pretty poor.  I can get pretty much anything I want at local Carquests, NAPA, Murrays, Autozones, etc.||||reg||1
